_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 7
---
order: 7
---
short_label: VII.7
---
statement: If a number is that part of a number which a subtracted number is of a subtracted number, then the remainder is also the same part of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.
---
proof:

Let the number *AB* be that part of the number *CD* which *AE* subtracted is of *CF* subtracted.

I say that the remainder *EB* is also the same part of the remainder *FD* that the whole *AB* is of the whole *CD.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="300" height="120" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.7 diagram" src="propVII7.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VII.7",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,80;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,80;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,120,40",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,195,40",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "C;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,120,80",
            "D';point;cutoff;C,C3,A,B;0;0",
            "D;point;cutoff;D',C3,A,B",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "E;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,150,40",
            "F';point;cutoff;C,C3,A,E;0;0",
            "F;point;cutoff;F',C3,A,E",
            "G;point;cutoff;C,C0,F,D",
            "GC;line;connect;G,C"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let *EB* be the same part of *CG* that *AE* is of *CF.*

Now since *EB* is the same part of *CG* that *AE* is of *CF,* therefore *AB* is the same part of *GF* that *AE* is of *CF.* [!just VII.5]

But, by hypothesis, *AB* is the same part of *CD* that *AE* is of *CF,* therefore *AB* is the same part of *CD* that it is of *GF.* Therefore *GF* equals *CD.*

Subtract *CF* from each. Then the remainder *GC* equals the remainder *FD.*

Now since *EB* is the same part of *GC* that *AE* is of *CF,* and *GC* equals *FD,* therefore *EB* is the same part of *FD* that *AE* is of *CF.*

But *AB* is the same part of *CD* that *AE* is of *CF,* therefore the remainder *EB* is the same part of the remainder *FD* that the whole *AB* is of the whole *CD.*

Therefore, *if a number is that part of a number which a subtracted number is of a subtracted number, then the remainder is also the same part of the remainder that the whole is of the whole.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
---
body:

This proposition is like @VII.5 except it deals with subtraction instead of addition. It says division distributes over subtraction. Algebraically,

<center><i>b/n</i> – <i>e/n,</i> = (<i>b</i> – <i>e</i>)/<i>n.</i></center>

This proposition is used in the next proposition and in @VII.11.
